    "narrative": "The heart of our lineup today is anchored by **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Josh Naylor**, our two strongest starts with efficiency scores of 69.49 and 64.20, respectively. **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Rocker, where a 4.30 xERA and a positive platoon edge provide the necessary ceiling to drive our RBI production. Meanwhile, **Josh Naylor** finds himself in a high-leverage spot against Ryne Nelson; despite a slight park penalty, his strong dynamic platoon split and high batting order slot make him a plug-and-play cornerstone. **James Wood** remains a vital inclusion at 62.98; while he faces a stingy opponent in King, his elite sprint speed and aggressive order placement at leadoff keep him locked in as we hunt for scarce stolen bases.\n\nWe are navigating several high-risk slots today due to pending lineups. **Corbin Carroll** sits at a 59.57, just shy of our \"Strong\" threshold, as he contends with Woo\u2019s 3.43 xERA, though his #2 spot keeps his value buoyant. The most difficult personnel decision was managing the lower end of our starting nine, specifically regarding **Jose Caballero** and **Cole Young**. **Jose Caballero** is barely hanging on with a 47.78, hampered by a bottom-of-the-order assignment that suppresses his potential. **Tyler Soderstrom** barely edged out other depth pieces with a 53.16 score, largely because his park environment against a left-handed pitcher outweighs the concerns of the matchup. With **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Austin Riley**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** all sidelined by injury or rest, our bench depth is currently non-existent; we are forced to rely on the current configuration regardless of the risks posed by Woo's pitching profile.\n\nWe will monitor the official lineups closely for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Jose Caballero**, as any shift from our assumed batting orders will trigger an immediate reassessment of their utility. While we possess speculative depth in **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Henry Bolte**, none currently project better than our active starters. Should **Travis Bazzana** struggle to solve Gray, we lack the immediate bench maneuverability to pivot, making this a \"start-and-pray\" slate for the back half of our middle infield.",
